      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.27,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "Now for sending an HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 6.56,
          "en": "we can use the fetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.56,
          "end": 10.82,
          "en": "That's a default JavaScript function built into JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.82,
          "end": 12.55,
          "en": "It has nothing to do with react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.55,
          "end": 15.118,
          "en": "It's a standard JavaScript function supported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.118,
          "end": 16.91,
          "en": "in modern browsers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.91,
          "end": 21.83,
          "en": "and it is a function that allows us to send HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.83,
          "end": 26.29,
          "en": "We could also use third-party packages like axios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.29,
          "end": 30.58,
          "en": "which has all the popular library for sending HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.58,
          "end": 33.24,
          "en": "But I don't want to install an extra library here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.24,
          "end": 35.9,
          "en": "So I'll stick to fetch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.9,
          "end": 38.26,
          "en": "Now fetch wants an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.26,
          "end": 40.63,
          "en": "and the first argument should be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.63,
          "end": 44.98,
          "en": "It should be the URL to which we wanna to send a request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.98,
          "end": 47.96,
          "en": "And here that states URL which we get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.96,
          "end": 51.193,
          "en": "from the Firebase real-time database console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.35,
          "end": 56.43,
          "en": "Now this Firebase real-time database service works such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.43,
          "end": 60.91,
          "en": "that this URL can be manipulated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.91,
          "end": 64.51,
          "en": "We can add segments after this domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.51,
          "end": 68.77,
          "en": "And then these segments will be translated into folders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.77,
          "end": 71.4,
          "en": "You could say in your database into tables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.4,
          "end": 74.67,
          "en": "you could say, so we could send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 78.9,
          "en": "to this URL/meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 78.9,
          "end": 83.1,
          "en": "And that would add a meetups table, a meetups collection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 85.083,
          "en": "to that database here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.67,
          "end": 88.12,
          "en": "And hence, I'll do that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.19,
          "end": 92.93,
          "en": "Now, one special thing about this Firebase API is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.93,
          "end": 96.03,
          "en": "that you need to add dot json at the end here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.03,
          "end": 97.8,
          "en": "That's not react specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.8,
          "end": 100.543,
          "en": "That's just something Firebase requires.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.72999999999999,
          "end": 102.66,
          "en": "And with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.66,
          "end": 106.663,
          "en": "that is the URL to which we're sending our request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.53999999999999,
          "end": 111.55,
          "en": "But here I actually wanna store data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.55,
          "end": 114.312,
          "en": "on Firebase servers and to signal to Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.312,
          "end": 118.93,
          "en": "and to this API that we want to store data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.93,
          "end": 122.57,
          "en": "we actually must send a post request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.57,
          "end": 126.24,
          "en": "and by default fetch sends a get request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.24,
          "end": 130.04,
          "en": "And that will always depend on the API you're working with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.04,
          "end": 132.59,
          "en": "But most APIs are built such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.59,
          "end": 136.833,
          "en": "that storing data requires post requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.79,
          "end": 140.67000000000002,
          "en": "Now to send a post instead of a get request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.67000000000002,
          "end": 143.65,
          "en": "we add a second argument to fetch here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.65,
          "end": 147.3,
          "en": "And that second argument is an object which allows us to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 149.71,
          "en": "configure this fetch function call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.71,
          "end": 152.88,
          "en": "and this HTTP request, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.88,
          "end": 155.5,
          "en": "and here in this object we can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.5,
          "end": 158.76,
          "en": "set a method property to define the age",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 158.76,
          "end": 161.5,
          "en": "to DB method that will be used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.5,
          "end": 164.083,
          "en": "And here we can set this to post instead of get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.083,
          "end": 167.15,
          "en": "which would be the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.15,
          "end": 169.263,
          "en": "So here we use post instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.27,
          "end": 172.62,
          "en": "Now, when we send a post request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.62,
          "end": 175.62,
          "en": "we should also add the data to the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.62,
          "end": 177.79,
          "en": "the data which we wanna store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.79,
          "end": 180.77,
          "en": "And we do that through the body field, which we add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
